      "end_seconds": 17.7,
      "duration_seconds": 17.32,
      "text": "Doctor, my father, he is Polish, his English is good but when he is nervous he goes to Polish, so I will start. He sees two of everything in the evenings. Dwoje, he says."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 26.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Dwoje. Two. Double, double. In the evening, the television, two."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.36,
      "end_seconds": 35.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Thank you both. Mr Kowalczyk, how long has this been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.34,
      "end_seconds": 41.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Two months. Since the, the autumn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 42.95,
      "end_seconds": 51.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "Papa, it is longer. It was before the wedding in June. That is four months at least."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.91,
      "end_seconds": 58.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Two to four months, then. Is it one eye or both?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.46,
      "end_seconds": 65.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "When I close one eye, one picture. So both eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.26,
      "end_seconds": 70.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "What else do you notice?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 73.26,
      "end_seconds": 82.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "His right eyelid, it droops by the end of the day. Like he is sleepy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.74,
      "end_seconds": 87.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "My eyes are tired. Heavy, by evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.07,
      "end_seconds": 93.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Any other muscles that get tired?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.01,
      "end_seconds": 100.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Chewing. A steak, I must stop and rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 102.16,
      "end_seconds": 109.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "And his voice goes quiet at night, I can't hear him on the phone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.09,
      "end_seconds": 115.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Understood. Which tablets do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.73,
      "end_seconds": 130.36,
      "duration_seconds": 13.63,
      "text": "Bisoprolol, 5 mg, in the morning. And a small white pill for the thyroid, I do not know the name, in Polish I know it, here no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 132.32,
      "end_seconds": 136.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I can bring the box on Monday. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.07,
      "end_seconds": 142.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "That would help. Any allergies, Mr Kowalczyk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.27,
      "end_seconds": 152.32,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "In the hospital, a long time ago, some injection, I had a rash, I think. Which injection, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.99,
      "end_seconds": 159.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I'll note a possible allergy, unconfirmed. Medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.96,
      "end_seconds": 165.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "High blood pressure. The thyroid, underactive. And cataracts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.56,
      "end_seconds": 168.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.94,
      "end_seconds": 175.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Right eye, cataract, in 2019. And the hernia, 2011."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.22,
      "end_seconds": 181.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "What did you do for work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.56,
      "end_seconds": 186.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Electrician, forty years. Retired."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.34,
      "end_seconds": 191.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Who do you live with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 193.26,
      "end_seconds": 198.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "With me, and my family, since mama died."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.1,
      "end_seconds": 225.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "Let me check you. Blood pressure 138 over 80, pulse 62, temperature 36.6, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 14, weight 79 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 226.6,
      "end_seconds": 229.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Is the pulse low? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.32,
      "end_seconds": 254.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.31,
      "text": "It's on the slow side because of the bisoprolol. Now, Mr Kowalczyk, look up at my finger and keep looking, don't look away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.2,
      "end_seconds": 259.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Up. Up. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.62,
      "end_seconds": 266.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "After about a minute, the right upper eyelid droops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 268.08,
      "end_seconds": 270.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Yes! That is it! ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.18,
      "end_seconds": 284.56,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "And when I ask you to look to the side, you start with one picture, then a second one appears after a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.89,
      "end_seconds": 289.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Yes, it comes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.85,
      "end_seconds": 310.6,
      "duration_seconds": 18.75,
      "text": "Here is my thinking. Droopy eyelid, double vision and weakness that all get worse with tiredness is a pattern I take seriously. I can't rule out a condition where nerves and muscles don't communicate properly, called myasthenia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 312.61,
      "end_seconds": 315.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Is it serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.67,
      "end_seconds": 327.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "It's treatable, but I'd like to be careful. I'd like to arrange a blood test for the antibodies linked to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.76,
      "end_seconds": 333.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "When do I know? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.9,
      "end_seconds": 343.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "A week or so. I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 344.54,
      "end_seconds": 350.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Two weeks. I will bring him and the box. ~"
    }
  ]
